=head1 NAME

notify-osc - implement OSC notifications for urxvt

=head1 DESCRIPTION

This extension implements an OSC sequence handler for urxvt that
triggers desktop notifications using C<notify-send> and sets the
urgent hint of the terminal window.

=head1 OSC FORMAT

The OSC sequence must be:

  notify;summary;body

=head2 Example

  printf '\e]777;notify;Build finished;All tests passed\a'

The first field is the notification title (summary).
The second field is the notification body.

If the body is omitted, an empty string is used.

Example with empty body:

  printf '\e]777;notify;Hello world;\a'

=head1 Escaping

Semicolons inside fields must be escaped using C<\;>:

  notify;summary;body with \; semicolon

=head1 BEHAVIOR

- Runs asynchronously (does not block urxvt)
- Strips control characters from input
- Trims leading/trailing whitespace
- Ignores empty summaries
- Sets the terminal urgent hint
- Uses C<notify-send> for desktop notifications

=head1 Debugging

Debug output can be enabled via urxvt resource:

  URxvt.notify.debug: 1

When enabled, parsing and execution details are printed to STDERR.

=head1 DISPLAYING A NOTIFICATION

To test the OSC handler inside urxvt:

  printf '\e]777;notify;Test notification;Hello world\a'

=head1 REQUIREMENTS

C<notify-send> is used to create desktop notifications.

It is typically provided by the C<libnotify-bin> package
on Debian-based systems.

